redfin 1235: screen-off Touch ID wake: a finger on the sensor with the display off presses the power button, kern.sweet_mesa_wake (default 0)

iOS 16.7 matches only while the screen is on (SBUIBiometricResource: matching allowed = capability && screen on) and
SpringBoard turns background finger detect off (69 val 0) before the display goes off; on an iPhone 8 the wake is the
home button press and the screen-on match op then matches the resting finger. Here a sweetfpcd FINGER_DOWN while
iOS's display is off (SweetFramebuffer RequestPowerChange -> sweet_mesa_display) is that press: kern.sweet_mesa_wake
bit 0 posts a power button press (bit 1: home instead), not within kern.sweet_mesa_wake_ms (200) of the display going
off, at most one per 1.5 s; bit 2 posts FPCD_CMD_WAKEDET {on} to sweetfpcd on display off/on so it arms the sensor.
sweet_fpc.c: kern.sweet_fpc_wait_edge, an interrupt-only wait (level high / new gpio112 irq / kick, no 5 ms poll),
write 0 = kick. kern.sweet_mesa_wake_state: counters. Default 0: nothing changes (FINGER_DOWN, statuses, waits as before).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvAC4dCbJuYfzxCtCk4D8
